  "02:45 — 观察者席的扶手留下历代裁决者按住笔的凹痕。": "02:45 — The observer's chair-arm bears the dents where generations of arbiters pressed down their pens.",
  "03:58 — 零号钥匙打开出口，却没有自动选择应该通过的人。": "03:58 — The zero key opens the exit, yet does not automatically choose who should pass.",
  "05:13 — 十二位诺亚把各自名字签在同一只黄铜票夹里。": "05:13 — The twelve Noas sign their own names into one and the same brass ticket clasp.",
  "未成线不是镜子里的仓库。十二位诺亚在这里生活了不同长度的时间：有人修过屋顶，有人欠下图书馆罚款，有人已经成为替后来者标路的调查员。观察者席记录了仪式真正的开关——只要一位被认可的裁决者宣布谁是原本，其余人生就会被现实排除。零号钥匙只负责开门，从不负责选人。选择被写进了椅子，而不是镜子。": "The unmade line is no warehouse inside a mirror. Twelve Noas have lived here for different lengths of time: one has mended a roof, one owes a library fine, one has already become an investigator marking routes for those who come after. The observer's chair records the ritual's true switch — the moment a recognised arbiter declares who is the original, every other life is excluded by reality. The zero key only opens doors; it never selects people. The choice was written into the chair, not the mirror.",
  "如果镜子会自动选出唯一真身，终灯会为什么还要为外部观察者保留一张裁决席？": "If the mirror automatically selects a single true self, why does the Afterlight Society still keep a verdict seat for an outside observer?",
  "拒绝唯一原本": "Refuse a Single Original",
  "十三位千早诺亚在黎明前签下十三种名字，等待调查者决定是否仍要替她们选择。": "Thirteen Chihaya Noas sign thirteen names before dawn, waiting to see whether the investigator will still choose for them.",
  "城市愿意承认十三张车票，却坚持同一个名字只能兑换一份清晨。": "The city is willing to recognise thirteen tickets, yet insists one name may be redeemed for only one morning.",
  "证据应当公开、封存，还是把名字与去留权交还给十三位当事人？": "Should the evidence be made public, sealed, or should the name and the right to stay or go be returned to the thirteen themselves?",
